this is your first time doing a series  like this  and i'm curious what it was about the  material that said i want to spend  possibly the next four to seven years of  my life making this  you just said four to seven years and  almost fell out of my chair  um  no it what it was was you know we're  huge yellowstone fans and a big taylor  sheridan fan and you know wind river  sicario  hell or high water all the stuff that  he's written  but we were yellowstone fans from the  very first night of the very first  episode and  when all this came around and taylor  started sending scripts to us it  literally was the most beautiful  thing i've i've ever read i mean the  scripts are just so fantastic it just  jumps off the page at you and makes  everything to come to life  when you read it  you picture the entire show and the way  he describes everything and the way he  describes every scene  it's literally a road map for the dp  it's a road map for the set designers  it's a road map for everybody that's  involved  it's all there and all you have to do is  read the script and and you're inspired  by it and that's that's literally what  did it i mean  i wasn't looking for a series to do i  mean gosh i mean i got plenty of other  things to do i mean i wasn't even  looking for a movie to do and um  but but as an artist everything's driven  by the material that's put in front of  you and when when this kind of material  is putting in put in front of you and  it's a challenge and it's something that  you really  are moved by it's it's hard to say no to  i one of the things about this series is  that it's not a soundstage series this  is you guys really on location making it  and i can only imagine the challenges  for not only the cast but the crew in  trying to bring this to life can you  sort of talk about um just the behind  the scenes of the making of the series  and how what how tough it must be yeah  well the crew in particular  i mean they certainly have it a lot  tougher than than the actors do i mean  they the stuff that they have to move  and the elements that they have to move  it in when you even switching locations  within an hour in montana with 30 mile  an hour winds and you know 15 degree  temperatures i mean it's just almost an  impossible task and the wranglers  because we have  you know a herd of cattle we have  you know 50 horses you know all that  stuff that's involved in moving a set  there it's remarkable to me to me to  watch those guys work and i have nothing  but respect for all of them um but yeah  the elements are the toughest part i  mean we  knock on wood we've been fairly lucky i  mean we've we've been burning up when it  was early on and we've been freezing  cold and we've had a few days we had a  few decent days but most of the time  it's either been freezing cold or  burning hot then a couple days it was  both so it's just it's it's been a  challenge but  i think all of that i mean the elements  the the  the scenery  all of that is is a huge character in  this movie as well so i it adds to the  the the  authenticity of it i think  what are you uh my last question for you  um what are you most excited for people  to actually see in the series because i  think taylor just does such a tailor  does such a great job at making you  realize how rough and tough that time  period was  yeah i think for what we did with this  show is really tried to take the veneer  off of of the and the romanticism out of  of how how tough it was because you know  it's easy to watch westerns to think oh  i'd love to live during that time and  then when you see  see how tough it was you're like man  maybe i wouldn't but um  yeah i but for me i think that  honestly speaking and this is coming  from  my other life honestly speaking i can't  wait for people to see my wife and her  performance  in this show i think that she just  knocks it out of the park and  we have always known in our family that  she's the steel and the backbone of our  family and without her our universe will  just fall apart  but i think she's carried that over into  margaret's character and you see that in  margaret's character that she she's  she's the rock that holds everybody in  place yeah i think the two of you  together are also real good  i just want to say congrats i know the  show is going to be a big hit thank you  for giving me your time my pleasure  thank you
 

